message.content:
This is a CBP ruling on a mixture of surfactants, solvent, and oils used as a pharmaceutical compounding base. It is not a medicament put up in measured doses or retail packaging, and it has no stated therapeutic or prophylactic use by itself. Heading 3003 covers medicaments of mixed products for therapeutic use not in dosage form, but the base has no active ingredient. The better fit is heading 3824, chemical preparations not elsewhere specified, or possibly 3402 for organic surface-active preparations.

The product is a self-emulsifying preconcentrate, so 3402 is plausible, but its surfactants form only part of the mixture. The oil and solvent components point toward 3824. I recall the ruling as classifying it under 3824.99, with the subheading for other chemical products and preparations. For the statistical suffix I am using 3824.99.9298, a recalled "other" number that I have not verified.

{"hts_code": "3824.99.9298", "reason": "A mixture of surfactants, solvent, oils and preservatives used as a pharmaceutical compounding base is a chemical preparation not elsewhere specified or included, classified in heading 3824 as an 'other' product."}
